  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They led until the fourth inning, then couldn't finish it.",
    "what_this_means": "Ty France gave them a chance in the eighth with a two-run home run that pulled them within one, but it wasn't enough to overcome what Griffin Canning gave up in the fourth. The bullpen limped through. Matsui held the line in the sixth, Waldron kept it close with two clean innings. But the damage was done early. They had runners in scoring position six times and converted two of those chances into runs. That's not a collapse. That's a team that played well enough to stay in it and still came up short. This is what fragile looks like: close enough to win, but winning requires everything to align. France delivered when they were down to their last swing, but the math was already against them by then.",
